<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagorno-Karabakh Autonomous Oblast</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a>–<a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> Autonomous Oblast was an autonomous region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> SSR, created in 1923 for the mountainous part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a>, which had an Armenian majority. Its demand in 1988 for transfer to Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> began the Karabakh conflict. Azerbaijan abolished the oblast in November 1991, after the region had proclaimed itself the Nagorno-Karabakh Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh-autonomous-oblast.jpg" alt="Nagorno-Karabakh Autonomous Oblast" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagorno-Karabakh_AO_in_the_Soviet_Union_(European_part).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
